                         GSX Patch Disk


The GSX Patch Disk contains the necessary files for patching the
PC DOS versions of DR DRAW and DR GRAPH to run under Concurrent
PC DOS. To  use this disk follow the directions listed below.

Directions

	1.   Boot your system under Concurrent PC DOS.
	2.   Place the GSX Patch Disk in drive A.
	3.   Be sure you graphics package is on drive C
	     under the PC DOS partition.
	4.   Type the batch file name that you require
             followed by C:

Batch file names
	FIXDRAW - Fixes either the 8086 or the 8087 version
		  of DR DRAW.
	FIXGP192 - Fixes the 192K, 8086 version of DR GRAPH.
	FIXGP87 - Fixes the 192K, 8087 version of DR GRAPH.
	FIXGP128 - Fixes the 128K version of DR GRAPH.

EXAMPLE:

	If you have the 8086 or the 8087 version of DR DRAW, 
	type the following:

	A>FIXDRAW C:     (return)

You may now operate your graphics packages under Concurrent PC DOS,
they may be accessed from drive C:.
